  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1201 AM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nWeekend...HOT. Max temps will be 95 to 105+ across all of the plains \nboth days. The SLV and Mid/upper Ark Rvr valley will see low 90s. It \nwill be mainly dry Saturday (isold along NM border) but we may see a \nslightly better chance of high elevation convection on Sunday as the \nmonsoon moisture slowly creeps back into the mtns. Hot Weather \nHighlights (Heat Advisories) will likely be needed for both days \nacross the plains and possibly valleys these two days. W may also \nneed some Fire Weather Hilites over the far eastern plains both days \ndue to winds and low RH.\n\nMonday and Tuesday...moisture will be on the increase each day and \nwe will see pops start to climb up as the week progresses. Temps \nwill also slowly start to cree downwards, although I expect Lamar/LHX \nregions may see max temps reach 3 digit figures each of these days.\n\nWed into late week...concern is increasing that we will see a wet \nperiod over potentially all of the region as ensemble guidance shows \nQPF values increasing on most of the EC and GFS members, so \nconfidence is high that it will get wetter. The question is how much \nwetter will it get, as 6 hourly qpf values off he NBM gridded data \nare pretty high; more than half inch amounts; over parts of the \nregion WED, THU and FRI. We will have to start to watch for flash \nflooding potential all areas late next week, especially around the \nburn scars. \\/Hodanish",
